# Build context for backend/Dockerfile (context = repository root). The Dockerfile copies only
# pyproject.toml, uv.lock, backend/, rag/, agents/, memory/, integrations/, sample_data/ and database/,
# so everything else here is kept out of the context to keep it small and free of secrets and local data.
# The frontend image has its own context and its own frontend/.dockerignore.
.git
.githooks
.github
.claude
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
node_modules
**/node_modules
frontend
data/
*.db
.env
.env.*
CLAUDE.local.md
docs/plans
internal
tests
deployment
Screenshot*
.tmp*
*.tfstate
*.tfvars
backend.hcl
tfplan
